0..51 Comment "// This source models C strings from owned strings."
52..54 Comment "//"
55..132 Comment "// An owned string ends with one zero byte. The C standard reads this layout."
133..204 Comment "// Rust\'s `CStr` borrows the same layout. An interior zero prevents a C"
205..216 Comment "// reading."
217..219 Comment "//"
220..299 Comment "// `terminated` adds the final zero. `cView` borrows valid bytes without a copy"
300..318 Comment "// or re-encoding."
319..321 Comment "//"
322..345 Comment "// - cites: [Rust-CStr]"
346..348 Comment "//"
349..440 Comment "// [Rust-CStr]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ffi/struct.CStr.html \"Rust, CStr in std::ffi\""
